t\u201d yet they are scale one. So I\u2019m not sure how you can reall separate the two. <br /> Now having a bit of flex, becoming more flexible at higher scale makes some sense. Especially because bodies don\u2019t always perform the same day by day or even machines. Machines may have a more standard outcome results but they are not a 100% constant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6424-fuzzykuma","name":"Fuzzykuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-27T02:37:16-07:00","id":1332792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fuzzykuma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1331012-scales-in-numbers?p=1332772#post1332772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So two questions on the charts. What is Mm/h? I know it\u2019s something an hour but not sure what. <br /> <br /> Also shadowninja is the , meant to be a .? As in 1.25 tons? Or as 1 and 1/4 tons?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mm = Megameter, like a kilometer but 1000 times larger. So 1Mm/h is 1000km/h<br /> <br /> The \u201c,\u201d is working as a \u201c.\u201d In Latin America we use dot to break the thousands and coma to mark the decimals. It\u2019s the oficial way here, and even Excel works this way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-27T04:43:29-07:00","id":1332802,"title":"","content":"Mateus Luz is right, I used &quot;,&quot; as &quot;.&quot;.<br /> <br /> I am working in a new table using a few descriptions in the book (Core, Aeon and Aberrant) as reference. Example, in the Mega-Speed description states a sport-car as a Scale 4 and a supersonic speed as Scale 6 (Jet Fighter speed, the fastest Jet Fighter reaches 3000 km/h).<br /> To Lifting I think in another solution: create a relative scale similar to Speed Scale and Space Scale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/437-shadowninja","name":"shadowninja","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}